<html lang="en">
<head>
<title>Halloumi Burger With Wedges And Smoky Tomato Relish</title>
</head>
<body>
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Halloumi Burger With Wedges And Smoky Tomato Relish",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Gousto"
  },
  "description": "Packed with flavour, halloumi makes a brilliantly satisfying filling for a yummy vegetarian burger. Once you've fried slices of the halloumi till beautifully golden, you'll sandwich them into garlicky ciabatta along with a sweet, smoky tomato relish and a dressed salad. Hallelujah halloumi!",
  "image": "https://production-media.gousto.co.uk/cms/mood-image/865---Halloumi-Burger-With-Wedges-And-Smoky-Tomato-Relish2400-1692087524970-x1500.jpg",
  "recipeCategory": "Vegetarian",
  "recipeCuisine": "Mediterranean",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "Dried oregano (1tsp)",
    "Ground smoked paprika (1tsp)",
    "Ground smoked paprika (2tsp) x0",
    "Ciabatta x2",
    "Garlic clove",
    "Tomato x2",
    "Red wine vinegar (30ml) x0",
    "Halloumi (200g)",
    "Rocket (50g)",
    "Red wine vinegar (15ml)",
    "White potato x3"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 220°C/ 200°C (fan)/ gas 7 and boil a full kettle\nCut your potatoes (skins on) into wedges and add them to a baking tray (or two!) with a drizzle of vegetable oil\nSeason with a pinch of salt and pepper and sprinkle over your dried oregano, then put the tray[s] in the oven for 20-25 min or until the wedges are golden and crispy"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Meanwhile, slice your halloumi in half, lengthways (like you're slicing a burger bun!)\nAdd 500ml [750ml] [1L] boiled water to a wide-based deep pan and bring to the boil over a high heat\nOnce boiling, reduce the heat to medium, add the halloumi half[ves] and cook for 5-6 min or until softened"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Meanwhile, chop your tomato[es] finely\nPeel your garlic and chop in half, discard the skin\nChop (or grate) half the garlic finely (you'll use the rest later!)\nHeat a pot with a generous drizzle of olive oil over a medium heat"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Once hot, add the chopped tomatoes, chopped garlic, your ground smoked paprika and half your red wine vinegar (save the rest for later!) and cook for 2-3 min or until the tomato is starting to break down\nAdd 1 tbsp [1 1/2 tbsp] [2 tbsp] sugar and 2 tbsp [3 tbsp] [4 tbsp] water and increase the heat to medium-high\nCook for 5-8 min or until thickened to a chutney-like consistency – this is your smoky tomato relish"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Once softened, drain and pat the halloumi half[ves] dry with kitchen paper (save the pan!)\nUsing a rolling pin, flatten the halloumi half[ves] into a similar size as the ciabatta – this is your halloumi steak[s]"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Slice your ciabatta[s] in half, add to a separate baking tray (or two!) and drizzle with olive oil\nPut the tray[s] in the oven for 4 min or until slightly crispy, then remove from the oven and leave to cool\nCombine the remaining red wine vinegar with 2 tbsp [3 tbsp] [4 tbsp] olive oil and a pinch of salt and pepper– this is your dressing\nOnce cooled, rub the remaining garlic into the crispy ciabatta"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Once the potato wedges are nearly cooked, return the wide-based pan to a medium-high heat\nOnce hot, add the halloumi steak[s] to the pan and cook for 1-2 min on each side or until golden\nMeanwhile, wash your salad, then pat it dry with kitchen paper and toss it in the dressing"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "To assemble, fill the garlicky ciabatta with the halloumi steak and top with the smoky tomato relish and a handful of dressed salad – this is your halloumi burger\nServe the remaining dressed salad, any remaining smoky tomato relish and the wedges to the side\nEnjoy!"
    }
  ],
  "totalTime": "PT30M",
  "recipeYield": "2 servings",
  "nutrition": {
    "@type": "NutritionInformation",
    "calories": "636",
    "fatContent": "24.7g",
